    "title": "Evansville man charged with criminal gang intimidation - NewsBreak",
    "text": "By Andrew Newland ,\n2 hours ago\nEVANSVILLE, Ind. (WEHT) — An Evansville man has been charged with criminal gang intimidation.\nAn affidavit says on Tuesday, officers were called to Kentucky Avenue after a woman reported her car had been shot at. The victim told officers a black passenger car was followed her, then a skinny black male leaned out of the back passenger window and fired a gun at her car.\nOfficers say after speaking with the victim, they were able to identify the suspect as Vandan Chinn. The same day of the shooting, Chinn was live on Facebook rapping and holding a gun. Officers go on to say Chinn has been affiliated with gang activity for some time.\nChinn was arrested on Wednesday outside his residence without incident. He is charged with criminal gang control – criminal gang intimidation, unlawful carrying of a handgun and criminal recklessness with a deadly weapon.\nVandan Chinn Eyewitness News. Everywhere you are.\nCopyright 2026 Nexstar Media, Inc. All rights reserved. This material may not be published, broadcast, rewritten, or redistributed. For the latest news, weather, sports, and streaming video, head to Eyewitness News (WEHT/WTVW).",
    "summary": "(WEHT) — An Evansville man has been charged with criminal gang intimidation. An affidavit says on Tuesday, officers were called to Kentucky Avenue after a woman reported her car had been shot at. The victim told officers a black passenger car was followed her, then a skinny black male leaned out of the back passenger window and fired a gun at her car. Officers say after speaking with the victim, they were able to identify the suspect as Vandan Chinn. The same day of the shooting, Chinn was live on Facebook rapping and holding a gun.",
